- One major class per page; associated types and page-local argument/return types are extra `####` headings.
- Link parameter and return types. Types with their own page stay links only.
- Do not hand-write member tables; the transform builds them from `#####` members.
- Use `**Constructor**` / `**Properties**` / `**Methods**`.
- Rust may use `#### datasources` for free functions.
- Omit `bindInstall` / `bind_install`.
- The page-level selector switches both the class list and `::: example` samples.
- Under `## Examples`, use `::: example` pointing at unit, integration, or e2e test line ranges in all three languages. The transform extracts the usage body (not the test wrapper or equality asserts); do not paste fictional fences.
